Third-party components in the distributed model weights
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The model weights distributed for thesis/, paper/ and unified/ embed
tensors derived from torchvision's ImageNet-pretrained ResNets:

  thesis/  (artifacts/best_model_refit.pth): ResNet-18 (IMAGENET1K_V1) image
                 branch through layer4, initialised from the pretrained
                 weights and fine-tuned; its weights are derived from, not
                 copies of, the torchvision parameters, and its BatchNorm
                 running statistics, kept frozen, equal the pretrained ones
                 up to weight-EMA floating-point rounding (at most 2e-4
                 absolute).
  paper/   (artifacts/best_model_refit.pth): ResNet-18 (IMAGENET1K_V1) image
                 trunk through layer4, initialised from the pretrained
                 weights and fine-tuned; its weights are derived from, not
                 copies of, the torchvision parameters, and its BatchNorm
                 running statistics, kept frozen, equal the pretrained ones
                 up to weight-EMA floating-point rounding (at most 2e-4
                 absolute).
  unified/ (artifacts_voc/, artifacts_coco/): ResNet-50 (IMAGENET1K_V2)
                 trunk, frozen through layer2 (the pretrained parameters, up
                 to weight-EMA floating-point rounding, at most 6e-3
                 absolute) with later stages fine-tuned (derived).

Every other trained tensor is learned from scratch, not from pretrained
weights, by the code in each folder. Each folder's own NOTICE states the
details.

